--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/utils/busybox/patches/999-ash-clear-bb_got_signal-in-dotrap.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+From: dl12345 <https://forum.openwrt.org/t/mwan3-port-to-nftables/248270/404>
+Subject: [PATCH] ash: clear bb_got_signal in dotrap
+
+Busybox 1.38 introduced check_got_signal_and_poll() which is called before
+every builtin read. In a non-interactive script the bb_got_signal flag is
+never cleared after a signal handler fires, so any subsequent read spins
+forever at 100% CPU. Fix by resetting the flag in dotrap() once the signal
+has been dispatched, matching the behaviour that interactive shells get via
+the prompt display path.
+
+Affects any long-running script that traps signals and uses read: mwan3track,
+ddns-scripts, modemmanager, keepalived, acme-acmesh.
+
+--- a/shell/ash.c
++++ b/shell/ash.c
+@@ -9608,6 +9608,9 @@
+ 		savestatus = status;
+ 	}
+ 	pending_sig = 0;
++#if ENABLE_FEATURE_EDITING
++	bb_got_signal = 0;
++#endif
+ 	barrier();
